cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use breedsim-mcp in your work, please cite it as below. AlphaSimR is the
  simulation engine this server drives and must be cited separately — see
  references.
title: breedsim-mcp
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for breeding-scheme simulation, driving
  AlphaSimR through rpy2. It enforces one structural rule: a single simulation
  run is not a result, and the API will not return one. Every programme is run
  over a replicate floor and reported as a per-cycle mean, standard deviation and
  confidence interval, because the seed-to-seed spread of an identical scheme is
  the same order as the effects being compared. Paired A/B comparison uses common
  random numbers so shared luck cancels within the pair, and genomic selection is
  gated on measured founder linkage disequilibrium rather than on the name of the
  founder generator.
type: software
